o has this straight at a minimum. The only hand that beats me is if the opponent holds a King (making a King-high straight). Given the passive betting history (checks all the way down) and the opponent's check on the river, it is likely we will split the pot. Betting offers little value because better hands (Kx) will call or raise, and worse hands (which are impossible here since everyone has the straight) cannot call. Checking ensures I secure my share of the pot without risking a loss to a hidden King.\n\nReason: The board itself constitutes a made Straight (8 through Q). Since my hole cards do not improve this to a higher straight (I would need a King), and the opponent is guaranteed to have at least the same hand as the board, the best outcome I can reasonably expect is a split pot. Betting risks reopening the action against a potential King held by the opponent. Checking is the safest play to realize the split pot.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
